Module muster "The Long Muster's Road" {
  // ── Eleven hundred and four years, as the Annals keep them ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The valley's history goes beyond the company's visit: three years the Annals mark in red, each a quarrel that
  // made the valley what it is. They are told by the Archivist, one topic apiece, once he trusts the company; and
  // each leaves a custom in the valley that can be seen without being told.
  Relation annalsOpen(group).
  Discovery second_wife_known "In the year 212 the Prefect Aulus took a second wife from the Hearth while the first, an Eagle's daughter, still lived; the valley has eaten at two tables since.".
  Discovery plague_winter_known "In the year 640 a plague killed a third of the valley in a winter; the lot was drawn, and the courier died at the Sending gate, and since then the Sending goes out with a white cord at its wrist.".
  Discovery schism_known "In the year 871 the Eagles proposed to send the standard itself north with the Sending, to be nearer the Emperor; one night the gold wings were gone, and a brass eagle in a skin of bronze stood on the pole by morning. The Eagles said the Hearth had stolen them. A man was killed.".
  Discovery two_sendings_known "In the year 1002 the valley sent two couriers, one by the Eagles and one in secret by the Hearth; neither came home; neither is in the Annals but in the margin, as: both.".

  Topic moll_annals with moll "Ask the Archivist to open the Annals" when admitted(party) and not annalsOpen(party) once {
    Says "He lifts a book down that takes both arms, and lays it on the cedar, and opens it at no page in particular. 'Eleven hundred and four years,' says Moll. 'Most of it is the weather, and who was Prefect, and how many sacks. Four years are written in red. I shall tell you the red ones, if you will tell me something in return that I do not know.'".
    On discuss { Assert annalsOpen(party). }
  }
  Topic moll_wife with moll "Ask the Archivist about the year of the second wife" when annalsOpen(party) {
    Says "'The year two hundred and twelve,' says Moll. 'The Prefect Aulus was an Eagle, and his wife was an Eagle's daughter, and she was barren, or he thought she was. So he took a second wife from the Hearth, a farmer's girl with hips and hands and no Latin. And his first wife lived. And the valley divided into two tables.' He puts his finger on the line. 'The Prefect still eats at the Eagles' table one day and the Hearth's the next. It is the only law in the valley that no one remembers the reason for. It is also the only law no one has broken.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, second_wife_known). }
  }
  Topic moll_plague with moll "Ask the Archivist about the plague winter" when annalsOpen(party) {
    Says "'Six hundred and forty,' says Moll. 'One in three. The Sending was due at the spring and the lot fell on a girl of nineteen, and she walked out of the gate with the pouch and fell down dead on the path with her white cord on, and no one touched her for a day, for fear. The next year they drew again.' He shuts the book. 'Since then the courier wears a white cord, which is not for mourning. It is so the valley will know whose turn it was, if there is no one left to say.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, plague_winter_known). }
  }
  Topic moll_schism with moll "Ask the Archivist about the Schism of the Standard" when annalsOpen(party) {
    Says "'Eight hundred and seventy-one,' says Moll, in the voice of a man reading a charge sheet. 'A young Aquilifer proposed, in the evening call, that the standard itself be carried north with the Sending, to be put into the Emperor's hand. The Eagles roared. The Hearth was silent. In the night the wings were taken, and in the morning a brass eagle in a skin of bronze stood on the pole, and the Aquilifer, who loved the old bird more than his mother, hanged himself in the shrine.' He closes his eyes. 'There was fighting in the forum for three days. A man was killed. The Eagles have said ever since that the Hearth stole the gold, and the Hearth has said nothing at all, which is its way.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, schism_known). }
  }
  Topic moll_two with moll "Ask the Archivist about the year of two Sendings" when annalsOpen(party) and knows(actor, schism_known) {
    Says "'One thousand and two. Nobody knows, and I have been looking for thirty years,' says Moll. 'The Annals say the Eagles' courier went, as ever. But in the margin, in a hand I do not know, a single word: BOTH. A courier from the Hearth, who went by the Goat Path in the night.' He taps. 'Neither came home. It is the only year in the whole book in which two went north, and I think it is the year the Hearth first understood what the Eagles would not.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, two_sendings_known). }
  }
  Observe beam_scene at archive when true "A roof-beam of black cedar runs the length of the Archive, and cut along its underside, in small even notches grouped in fives, is a tally that goes from the north wall to the south. The last groups are fresh and pale. There are, you count idly, a great many.".
  Observe two_tables at praetorium_hall when knows(party, second_wife_known) "Two tables stand in the hall's end, set for a meal, one with red cloth and one with brown. The Prefect, you notice, is at the red one today.".
  Observe white_cord at gate as sign when knows(party, plague_winter_known) "On a peg inside the gate hangs a white cord, worn to a grey rope, waiting for the spring.".
  Observe schism_scar at forum when knows(party, schism_known) "On the paving at the foot of the standard's pole, worn nearly smooth, a darker patch the shape of a man lying. Nobody walks on it. Every child steps round it without thinking.".
}
